WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.850
With Avengers: Infinity War and Avengers:
Endgame, the last remnants of the walls dividing

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.320
the separate regions of the MCU were finally
obliterated once and for all.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:15.179
Now, Phase Four of the MCU is just around
the corner, and we've got a wish list of the

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.180
mash-ups we're most hoping to see.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:22.671
Sam Wilson, recently seen taking up Cap's
shield at the end of Avengers: Endgame, will

00:00:22.671 --> 00:00:28.269
be co-headlining the Disney+ series The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier with Sebastian Stan's

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:29.080
Bucky Barnes.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:34.640
Although Sam has shown up in three Avengers
movies, and briefly in Ant-Man, he's primarily

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.110
been a Captain America character, and hasn't
interacted much with many of the MCU's sprawling

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.200
roster of heroes.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.650
While there's no shortage of existing characters
Sam hasn't yet met, the one we'd most like

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.460
to see him interact with is Carol Danvers.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:53.760
Sam will be in the market for a new best friend
after losing Steve to the past in Endgame,

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.140
and we get the feeling Carol has been a little
personally unmoored ever since losing and

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.500
regaining her memories in Captain Marvel.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.760
They could each use a new shoulder to lean
on, and we can see their personalities playing

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.180
well off of one another.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.020
In addition to their shared military background,
Sam's experience running a support group for

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.240
veterans may be just what Carol needs to help
unpack all she's been through.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:20.070
What's more, their shared experience of losing
their best friends may help them understand

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.400
one another in a unique and interesting way.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.300
Although WandaVision has confirmed that Ant-Man
and the Wasp's FBI agent Jimmy Woo will be

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.900
appearing in some capacity, we have no idea
what sort of role he'll be playing in the

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.120
mind-bending tale.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:39.000
WandaVision is one of the least predictable
of the Disney+ shows since we've been told

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:43.590
that it'll take place after the events of
Avengers: Endgame, but also apparently in

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.780
the 1950s.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:50.900
As such, it's entirely possible that some
characters may exist in one time period or

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:56.520
reality, and not in others, meaning that there's
no guarantee that Wanda or Vision will actually

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.960
interact with every member of the show's cast.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:03.770
However, we really hope that we get to see
what happens when Jimmy encounters Vision

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:04.760
for the first time.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.980
It's not just that we want each of them to
make a good friend, although that's part of

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:09.480
it.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:15.460
Besides Wanda, Vision has always seemed kind
of isolated, and Jimmy came across as pretty

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.920
lonely in Ant-Man.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.500
"Did you want to grab dinner or something?

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.020
I mean, 'cause I'm… free."

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:26.780
We'd love nothing more than to see the two
of them buddy up and fill that bestie-shaped

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.080
hole in each other's lives.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.780
But also, given Jimmy's interest in Scott's
close-up magic tricks, we expect him to be

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:38.460
blown away by Vision's abilities, and really,
his entire half-technological, half-magical

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:38.960
existence.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.380
The ending of Doctor Strange pulled a first
for an MCU movie, laying the groundwork for

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.470
a character who had been an ally throughout
the entire film to become a villain in the

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:48.960
next one.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:54.480
So although Baron Mordo hasn't been confirmed
to appear in Phase Four, it would be surprising

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.720
if he didn't show up again.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:03:00.720
In fact, we think WandaVision would be a great
and unexpected place to bring him back.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:06.510
The rigidly principled Mordo spent most of
Doctor Strange growing increasingly uncomfortable

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:11.420
with the way that both Strange and the Ancient
One used magic, so we can't imagine he'll

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.000
react well to Wanda Maximoff and her reality-altering
powers.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:20.280
It would be a fascinating way to tie the worlds
of WandaVision and Doctor Strange together

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.480
- an event which has already been confirmed
to happen, one way or another.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:30.060
Perhaps Wanda creates some sort of alternate
reality where Vision is alive, splitting open

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:35.200
the multiverse and drawing Mordo's attention,
leading directly into the events of Doctor

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.600
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:42.320
Or maybe Mordo is already well on his way
down a dark path, and Wanda is the one who

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.500
discovers it, prompting her to seek help from
Doctor Strange.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:50.740
While the possibilities for who could make
a surprise appearance in Loki are nearly endless,

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:56.050
another name at the top of our list is Doctor
Strange's the Ancient One, who surprised audiences

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.020
by showing up in Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.930
She'd be the perfect one for Loki to meet
up with as he skips through time, especially

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.940
if he has an Infinity Stone in tow.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:10.140
In addition to providing some much-needed
exposition on how Loki's adventures may muddy

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:15.820
up the larger timeline, the Ancient One also
has the unique ability to see alternate futures.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:20.440
That means that although Loki will have no
knowledge of his character growth in Phases

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.280
Two and Three of the MCU, she very well could.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:29.560
Perhaps a meeting with the Ancient One will
be exactly what Loki needs in order to help

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.820
him become a better version of himself, putting
him on the path to becoming the kind of person

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.940
he was at the beginning of Infinity War.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.460
Along with the surprise announcement that
WandaVision would be bringing back Jimmy Woo

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.910
came the equally shocking revelation that
the series would also be pulling in the character

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.020
of Darcy Lewis from the first two Thor movies.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:54.100
Darcy was astrophysicist Jane Foster's intern,
although her political science major didn't

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.540
always make her the best fit for Jane's scientific
theorizing and experimentation.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:03.960
Like Jane, Darcy didn't appear in Thor: Ragnarok,
but now it appears she'll be returning for

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.020
WandaVision, although we have no idea how
or why.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:13.240
Since WandaVision is reported to lead directly
into Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.940
we are crossing our fingers that Darcy will
be coming along for the ride too.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:23.100
When and if she does, we hope she'll have
a chance to get to know Wong, Strange's long-suffering

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.220
friend and instructor in the Mystic Arts.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:31.540
Considering how Darcy always reacted to Thor's
magic-adjacent abilities, we suspect her reactions

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.820
to actual magic would be a comedic goldmine.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:40.380
Plus, Wong and Darcy both know how it feels
to be relegated to the sidekick, and we imagine

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:46.250
that Darcy's blunt honesty and abundant eccentricities
will provide an entertaining contrast to Wong's

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:48.840
deadpan demeanor and constant exasperation.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.280
Maybe they can go out for sandwiches together.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.440
"I wouldn't say no to a tuna melt."

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.400
Although the Spider-Man movies already contain
the vast majority of the teenage characters

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:04.900
in the MCU, Peter hasn't yet come face to
face with that other Marvel wunderkind, Wakanda's

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.740
princess and chief innovator, Shuri.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.800
The two were briefly in the same place at
the same time during Avengers: Endgame, but

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.240
as far as we know, they never interacted.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:18.600
All that could change in the MCU's Spider-Man
3, which will pick up on the heels of that

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.760
doozy of a cliffhanger at the end of Spider-Man:
Far From Home.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:26.600
Maybe Peter goes into hiding after his secret
identity is revealed, and winds up seeking

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:28.260
aid from the people of Wakanda.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.700
We'll accept any number of scenarios as long
as it brings two of the MCU's greatest young

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.000
scientific minds together for a few scenes.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:41.220
The opening of Avengers: Endgame gave us a
pairing we never really expected to see, as

00:06:41.221 --> 00:06:46.460
Tony Stark and Nebula made their way laboriously
back to Earth after finding themselves the

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:49.040
only survivors on Titan following the snap.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:54.040
The two proved to have a delightful dynamic,
and the quiet scenes of the two of them together

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.760
were surprisingly poignant.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:07:00.600
Nebula then went on to play one of the most
important roles in Endgame, and ended the

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:05.660
film back aboard the Benatar with the rest
of the Guardians of the Galaxy, minus Gamora,

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:06.420
plus Thor.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:11.300
Assuming they're still all traveling the stars
together as the Asgardians of the Galaxy at

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.760
the beginning of Thor: Love and Thunder, we
hope that Nebula gets a chance to interact

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:16.540
with Korg.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.310
Korg is still on Earth at the end of Endgame,
as part of the New Asgard settlement over

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:25.810
which Valkyrie rules as King, but we know
both characters are already confirmed for

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:26.950
Love and Thunder.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:31.740
While we have no such confirmation for Nebula
or the other Guardians, we wouldn't be surprised

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.840
if the crew of the Benatar appears for at
least part of the film, even if it's just

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:38.120
to drop Thor off before heading back out again.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:43.160
If they do, we're crossing our fingers for
some scenes between the aggressively self-serious

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.280
Nebula and the gentle-hearted, unflappable
Korg.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:51.000
We can't imagine what they'd talk about, but
it would surely be thoroughly entertaining.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.160
Maybe they can bond about how much they hate
their father figures?

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.400
"Well I tried to start a revolution, but didn't
print enough pamphlets, so hardly anyone showed

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.860
up except for my mum and her boyfriend, who
I hate."

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:07.140
Marvel and director Taika Waititi ruthlessly
cleaned house for Thor: Ragnarok, killing

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:11.919
off half of the supporting Asgardian characters
from the previous films and cutting the Earth-bound

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.860
characters out of the story entirely.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.080
However, one established Thor character whose
fate is still up in the air following the

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:23.700
events of Ragnarok, Infinity War, and Endgame
is Lady Sif.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:28.530
The character was last seen on the big screen
delivering the Reality Stone to the Collector

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:33.240
at the end of Thor: The Dark World, before
appearing in a couple of episodes of Agents

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:33.840
of SHIELD.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:39.520
Whether or not Sif was blipped by Thanos in
Infinity War, she should be alive by the time

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.500
Love and Thunder rolls around, and we're ready
for her to return to the MCU.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:48.480
Especially because we really want to see what
happens when Sif and Valkyrie finally meet

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:49.100
one another.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.720
It's high time that the Thor movies allowed
more than one powerful female warrior on the

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.940
thunder god's team at a time, and we imagine
that these two will really hit it off.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:02.720
Tessa Thompson has said that Valkyrie will
be in search of her queen, and Alexander has

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.680
volunteered herself for the role on Twitter.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:09.660
Whether or not a romantic relationship is
in the cards for the two Asgardian warriors,

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:12.480
we still expect some sparks to fly when they
finally come together.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:17.620
Although Bruce Banner and Jane Foster are
both gifted scientists who have played major

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:21.160
roles in previous Thor movies, their paths
have never crossed.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:26.880
By the time Bruce smashed his way into Thor:
Ragnarok, Jane and Thor had broken up, and

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.450
we thought she'd vanished from the MCU for
good.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:33.660
But now that we know Jane is returning for
Thor: Love and Thunder, we're anxious for

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:35.900
Bruce to make a return appearance as well.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:41.060
While earlier Thor movies have allowed Jane
to bounce her scientific ideas off of Erik

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:47.640
Selvig, we'd love a film in which she's allowed
to riff about quantum physics with Bruce instead,

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:49.480
especially if he's in his big green form.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:54.440
With Tony Stark gone, Bruce could use a new
partner to talk shop with, and we can't think

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:59.260
of a better person to speak the strange language
of science-meets-superheroes than Jane Foster.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:04.080
Although Clint Barton and Bucky Barnes have
both been around in the MCU since Phase One,

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.149
and even fought on the same team in Captain
America: Civil War, we still haven't seen

00:10:08.149 --> 00:10:10.220
the two actually interact with one another.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:15.080
It's an odd oversight, especially considering
that both were trained by branches of the

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:19.910
same organization, have a super-spy background,
and know what it feels like to have their

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:22.360
minds taken over by an external force.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:28.280
So while we still have no idea how much the
Disney+ shows will cross over with one another,

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:33.180
our hope is that the Hawkeye series will finally
bring the archer and the Winter Soldier together.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:37.140
Although Bucky and Clint have shared a lot
in common in the past, they've never been

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:40.300
more alike than they are in the post-Endgame
MCU.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:45.540
Clint spent the five years before the Time
Heist tracking down and killing people who,

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:50.120
while they weren't entirely innocent, likely
didn't deserve the fate he meted out to them.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:54.920
By the time he found himself on Vormir, Clint
felt significant remorse for the harm he had

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:55.420
done.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:00.200
No character in the MCU is better poised to
understand what that feels like than Bucky

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:04.300
Barnes, who spent 70 years as a brainwashed
Hydra assassin.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:09.420
If The Falcon and the Winter Soldier can work
in a crossover with Hawkeye, we expect these

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:14.630
two will have a lot to discuss...As long as
Bucky cares more than Black Panther did when

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:15.800
he and Clint finally met.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.600
"We haven't met yet.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:21.360
I'm Clint."

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:22.300
"I don't care."

